# M2.4 acceptance: zoom, navigation and current page on tests/data/long.pdf
# (520 US Letter pages, see tests/data/make_long_pdf.py). Every page shows
# "Page N of 520" in large type at the top, 25 lines
# "Line i of page N. The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog." and a blue
# circular line pattern in its lower half. Run with
#   scripts/shot.sh -o <repo>/.verify/m2.4/<impl|review|tester> -s tests/acceptance/m2.4.steps -- ./build/app/agentic-reader tests/data/long.pdf
#
# The Ctrl+wheel block at the end needs shot.sh steps `keydown <keysym>` and
# `keyup <keysym>` (xdotool keydown/keyup). Until shot.sh has them, the run stops
# there with "unknown step: keydown" after shots 01-24 are written.
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent:
#   - MainFrame::CreateToolBar() directly under the menu bar, left to right:
#     zoom combo (editable wxComboBox, 100px wide), "Fit Width" and "Fit Page"
#     (text-labelled buttons or text-only tools), a separator, the page entry
#     (wxTextCtrl, 60px wide) and a label "/ M", so the pair reads "12 / 520".
#     Click points below: combo text (35,48), Fit Width (148,48),
#     Fit Page (234,48), page entry (320,48).
#   - The zoom combo always shows the effective zoom as a whole percent, e.g.
#     "119%" in fit width mode. Typing a plain number ("200") and Enter sets that
#     percent. Typing a page number in the page entry and Enter jumps to it.
#   - The go-to-page box (Ctrl+G) accepts typed digits and Enter, with its text
#     selectable by Ctrl+A (a wxTextEntryDialog, or focusing the page entry).
#   - A jump (Ctrl+G, page entry, Home) puts the target page's top edge at the
#     top of the pane (at y 69, or y 81 with the 12px gap above it).
#   - Zoom from the keys and the combo keeps the document point at the pane
#     center fixed (zoomScrollOrigin with anchor = pane center, see
#     tests/test_pdf_view_nav.cpp). Fit Page also scrolls so the current page is
#     fully in view, its top edge 12px below the pane top.
#   - Ctrl+wheel: one notch is one 10% step, anchored at the cursor.
#
# Geometry at the default 1400x900 window: menu bar y 0..27, toolbar y 28..68,
# PDF pane x 225..980 and y 69..875 (client 755x806), status bar y 876..900.
# Pane center is (602,472). Fit width = (755 - 24) / 612 = 119.4% (page 731px
# wide, 946px tall, x 237..968). Fit page = (806 - 24) / 792 = 98.7% ("99%").
# All y values below assume this toolbar height. If the toolbar is a few pixels
# taller or shorter, every pane y shifts by the same amount.
wait 3

# Toolbar under the menu bar: zoom combo, "Fit Width", "Fit Page", page entry
# "1" with "/ 520" after it. Page 1 is at the top of the PDF pane with its
# "Page 1 of 520" heading. Status bar (bottom left) shows the file name
# "long.pdf" (a path ending in long.pdf is also fine). The zoom combo value
# matches the page width on screen (page width / 612).
shot start

# Focus the PDF view. The combo may hold focus at startup.
click 600 500
key ctrl+0
wait 2

# Ctrl+0 resets to fit width: combo "119%". Page 1 spans the pane width minus
# 12px grey margins (about x 237..968), top edge at about y 81.
# "Line 25 of page 1" sits at about y 647..659. Entry "1 / 520".
shot ctrl0-fit-width

key Down Down Down Down Down
wait 1

# Down x5 scrolls 200px (40px each): everything sits exactly 200px higher than
# in ctrl0-fit-width, "Line 25 of page 1" at about y 447..459. Entry "1 / 520".
shot down-x5

key Up Up
wait 1

# Up x2 scrolls back 80px: everything sits 120px higher than in
# ctrl0-fit-width, "Line 25 of page 1" at about y 527..539. Entry "1 / 520".
shot up-x2

key Home
key Next
wait 2

# PgDn scrolls one viewport (806px) from the top. The lower ~150px of page 1
# (bottom of its blue pattern and its bottom edge at about y 221), the grey gap,
# then page 2 from about y 233 with "Page 2 of 520". Entry "2 / 520": page 2 has
# more visible area than page 1, although page 1 is the page at the top.
shot pgdn

key Next
wait 2

# Another viewport down. Page 2's lower part ends at about y 373, page 3 starts
# at about y 385 with "Page 3 of 520". Entry "3 / 520" (page 3 shows ~490px,
# page 2 ~304px).
shot pgdn-again

key Prior
wait 2

# PgUp scrolls one viewport back: identical to pgdn. Entry "2 / 520".
shot pgup

key End
wait 3

# End: the bottom of page 520 with its blue pattern, its bottom edge at about
# y 863 and the 12px grey margin below it. "Line 1 of page 520" is near the top
# of the pane (about y 82). The heading is above the pane (the page is taller
# than the pane at fit width). Entry "520 / 520".
shot end

key Home
wait 3

# Home: identical to ctrl0-fit-width. "Page 1 of 520" at the top, entry "1 / 520".
shot home

key ctrl+g
wait 1

# Ctrl+G opened a go-to-page box with keyboard focus, ready for a page number.
shot goto-box

key ctrl+a
type 250
key Return
wait 3

# The box is closed. Page 250's top edge is at the top of the pane (y 69..81)
# with "Page 250 of 520" below it. Entry "250 / 520". Status bar still shows
# "long.pdf". The pane center (602,472) lies on the word "over" in Line 14 or
# Line 15 of page 250. Later zoom shots keep that word at the center.
shot goto-250

click 35 48
key ctrl+a
type 100
key Return
wait 3

# Combo zoom: combo "100%". Page 612px wide (about x 296..908). The word "over"
# of the same line of page 250 is still at the pane center. Entry "250 / 520".
shot combo-100

click 600 500
key ctrl+plus
key ctrl+plus
wait 3

# Ctrl++ twice: combo "120%", page about 734px wide. Same word at the pane
# center. Entry "250 / 520".
shot ctrl-plus-x2

key ctrl+minus
wait 3

# Ctrl+- once: combo "110%", page about 673px wide. Same word at the pane
# center. Entry "250 / 520".
shot ctrl-minus

key --repeat 12 --repeat-delay 50 ctrl+minus
wait 4

# Zoom out clamps at 25%: combo "25%", not lower. Pages are about 153x198px,
# about four stacked in the pane, all rendered. The pane center lies in page
# 250's block of text lines. Pages 249, 250 and 251 are fully visible and tie on
# area, so the entry shows the lowest: "249 / 520".
shot min-zoom

key --repeat 80 --repeat-delay 30 ctrl+plus
wait 8

# Zoom in clamps at 800%: combo "800%", not higher. The pane shows a magnified
# part of page 250's text: a few words ("jumps over the lazy") of about seven
# lines between Line 11 and Line 18, each line about 80px tall, with the word
# "over" of the same line as in goto-250 at or near the pane center (rounding
# over 80 steps may drift it by up to 30px). The text is fully rendered and
# sharp, not a white placeholder and not a blurry upscale. Entry "250 / 520".
shot max-zoom

wait 4

# Rendering settled at 800%: identical to max-zoom. Any difference (a white
# page, half-drawn glyphs) means visible pages keep being evicted and
# re-rendered (the M2.3 cache budget note).
shot max-zoom-settled

click 234 48
wait 3

# Fit Page button: combo "99%". Page 250 fully visible, top edge at about y 81,
# bottom edge at about y 863, page about 604px wide and centered. The heading
# "Page 250 of 520" is visible. Entry "250 / 520".
shot fit-page

click 148 48
wait 3

# Fit Width button: combo "119%". Page spans the pane width minus 12px margins
# (about x 237..968). Page 250 still fills most of the pane. Entry "250 / 520".
shot fit-width

click 320 48
key ctrl+a
type 400
key Return
wait 3

# Page entry: page 400's top edge is at the top of the pane with
# "Page 400 of 520" below it. Entry "400 / 520". Status bar "long.pdf".
shot entry-400

click 600 500
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
click 600 500 5
wait 2

# Wheel scroll down 10 notches: the view moved down at least 100px from
# entry-400. The entry shows the page with the most visible area in this image
# (compare the visible heights of the pages; 401 with wx's default 60px per
# notch). Status bar still "long.pdf".
shot wheel-scrolled

key --repeat 40 --repeat-delay 33 Next

# Taken 0.3s after holding PgDn for about 1.3s (40 presses, about 34 pages). The
# entry already shows a page in the 430s that matches the page filling most of
# the pane in this image (give or take one page if the shot races a repaint).
# It does not still show 400 or 401: the entry updates while scrolling.
shot during-scroll

wait 2

# Settled: the entry exactly matches the page with the most visible area, and
# that page's heading or lines are in view. Status bar "long.pdf".
shot after-scroll

# Ctrl+wheel. Set 100% and jump to page 250 for a known position.
click 35 48
key ctrl+a
type 100
key Return
wait 2
click 600 500
key ctrl+g
key ctrl+a
type 250
key Return
wait 3

# Before Ctrl+wheel: combo "100%", page 250's top edge at the top of the pane.
# The point (596,365) lies on the word "over" in Line 11 or Line 12 of page 250.
# Note which line: the next two shots must show that same word at (596,365).
shot before-ctrl-wheel

keydown ctrl
click 596 365 4
click 596 365 4
click 596 365 4
keyup ctrl
wait 3

# Ctrl+wheel up 3 notches: combo "130%". The same word "over" of the same line
# of page 250 is still at (596,365), within 3px. The text around it is larger
# and the page wider than the pane. Entry "250 / 520".
shot ctrl-wheel-in

keydown ctrl
click 596 365 5
click 596 365 5
click 596 365 5
click 596 365 5
click 596 365 5
click 596 365 5
keyup ctrl
wait 3

# Ctrl+wheel down 6 notches: combo "70%", page about 428px wide and centered.
# The same word "over" of the same line of page 250 is still at (596,365),
# within 3px. Entry "250 / 520".
shot ctrl-wheel-out
